=base:main-content.cmark

# Changelog: tramaj-cli-rs

Release history of `tramaj-cli-rs`, the standalone Rust command-line interface over tramaj-rs. Releases happen when there are
major changes rather than on a schedule; each entry below is one version.
Every implementation has its own page like this one, and each page is
tagged so the site builds one Atom feed per implementation:
#changelog #rust #tramaj-cli-rs

=base:main-content.tramaj-doc
@version=import("changelog/version", {"package": "tramaj-cli-rs"})
.div(class: "changelog",
  $version({
      "version": "0.1.0",
      "date": "unreleased",
      "summary": "Rust port of tramaj-cli's Main.purs over the tramaj-rs crate.",
      "changes": [
          {
              "kind": "added",
              "text": "Template + JSON context evaluation and the \`analyze\` subcommands, as a single static binary."
          },
          {
              "kind": "changed",
              "text": "Numbers keep their type through the context and the output: \`3\` is an integer and \`3.0\` a float, and a whole-valued float is written with its fraction. An integer outside the signed 64-bit range is refused."
          },
          {
              "kind": "added",
              "text": "\`evaluate --arithmetic\` turns the arithmetic profile on for the run. Without it, an error names the flag when the program references an arithmetic builtin."
          },
          {
              "kind": "added",
              "text": "\`analyze arithmetic\` lists the arithmetic builtins a program and its libraries reference; \`analyze all\` carries the list under \`arithmetic\`."
          }
      ]
  }).rendered)

